- A row is a class of its own for the same reason a palette row is: a named sub
- view declared inside a keyed one is hoisted by `upper` into a property of the
- ROOT, without the key, so one editor would be shared by every row.
$bog_vmap_app_inspect_row $mol_view
	- Full signature as it is written in the source, `Menu_option*` and `click?`
	- included: the suffixes are the difference between a port and a keyed port.
	sign \
	- Empty on an own property, so the badge itself marks what is inherited.
	owner \
	inherited false
	value? $mol_tree2_empty
	binds /string
	nodes *
	keyed? false
	changeable? false
	drop? null
	sub /
		<= Head $mol_view
			sub /
				<= Sign $mol_view sub / <= sign
				<= Owner $mol_view sub / <= owner
				<= Tools $mol_view sub <= tools /
		<= Value $bog_vmap_app_inspect_value
			tree? <=> value?
			binds <= binds
			nodes <= nodes
	- Signature switches are offered on own properties only. An inherited port has
	- no declaration in this document to put a `*` or a `?` on, and writing one
	- would mean silently declaring an override the user never asked for.
	Key $mol_check
		title \*
		hint \Много значений по ключу
		checked? <=> keyed?
	Next $mol_check
		title \?
		hint \Изменяемое
		checked? <=> changeable?
	Drop $mol_button_minor
		title \✕
		hint \Убрать свойство из документа
		click? <=> drop?
	attr *
		^
		bog_vmap_app_inspect_row_inherited <= inherited
